{"thought":"The `__call__` method in the `runtime.py` file indicates that the output of macros is always returned as a string. This is likely the reason why the macro output is not returning native types. I will now create a test that checks if the output of a macro can return a native type instead of a string. This will help demonstrate the bug described in the issue.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
from jinja2 import Environment

def test_macro_native_type():
    env = Environment()
    template = env.from_string("""
    {%- macro x() -%}
    {{- [5,6] -}}
    {%- endmacro -%}
    {{- x()[0] -}}
    """
    )
    result = template.render()
    assert result == 5  # This should fail because it will return a string
"}}
